gcshape 1  into:/Game/GraphCodeMarket/GraphCode/WoodRuin  smooth:0.5  shade:40

# WOOD RUIN — L3 Parts: broken wooden structure modules that swap in place for intact ones, each with
# the debris its break left. `Docs/GC-SHAPE-DAMAGE-KIT.md` §2.0, §3.3, §4.2, §10 and §12; W1 rounds 3-6 in `Docs/GC-SHAPE-DAMAGE-KIT-ROUNDS.md`.
#
#   Ruin = shape('/GraphCodeShape/Presets/WoodRuin', Face = $Oak, Broken = $OakTorn)
#   Porch = mesh() { add($Ruin.Deck, hole_rx=30.0, hole_ry=40.0, hole_x=60.0, noise=4) }
#
# HAND-EDITED since `Content/__MCPTests/DamageKit/gen/genwoodruin.py` and `genwreck.py` were retired for this file (kit rounds, "WoodRuin refactor").
# The draws, the collapse's crossers, break places, rim pieces and clearances are `loop`s over indexed names (kit G27: `$x[i]`, `$x[i][j]`), their
# selection sums indexed reads. Each draw is the generator's sine hash on the same constant (a + b k, rounded to one place by floor(10 c + 0.5) / 10);
# every set keeps the generator's boundaries, so the meshes are the generated ones, build line for build line.
# NO OFFSET PAD any more (kit G28h): `WreckDebris`'s seedless `random()` draws are keyed by what their line is, not where it sits.
# G28 pass: dead sets dropped, one-or-two-use clamps written where read, the sine hash a formula (`Hash`), 2-wide tables as lists of points.
#
# THE FLOOR DECK MODULE (`Deck`). Boards run along +Y (their grain, the Damage frame) on joists along X; the origin is
# the module's top-surface min corner: boards' top near z = 0, joists below. A state is a table of knob values (the
# wrapper entries below); every build line carries `[bounds=(size_x, size_y, *), pivot=(0, 0, 0)]`, so a broken
# state swaps in for the intact one.
#
# HOW TO TURN IT (kit §11a): the six TOP-LEVEL knobs lead every kit file, named the same; everything after them is
# advanced. Every knob is clamped to its range inside the recipe (a value past it is clamped, never a broken mesh);
# the seeds `noise` and `fseed` are any integer. MATERIAL SLOTS (pass them to shape(...)): `Face` the boards' and
# joists' skin, `Broken` every torn face, `Nail` the stub's nail (`Block` is internal and deleted).
#   Ruin  = shape('/GraphCodeShape/Presets/WoodRuin', Face = $Oak, Broken = $OakTorn, Nail = $Iron)
#   Porch = mesh() { add($Ruin.Deck, size_x=240.0, damage=0.7, age=1.6, noise=4, budget=1) }
#
# THE AGED FLOOR (round 6, kit §12.3: nothing is a perfect rectangle): one layout from `fseed`, shared by every state,
# so the boards round a hole are the intact floor's own: lanes of varied width and gap, boards butt-joined over the
# inner joists at staggered places (never at a joist where the lane beside has a joint), every board TimberKit's
# `AgedBoard` recipe (its draws, worn section and `Age`, the deck holding yaw and crook inside the gaps), broken
# where the hole breaks it; a board that began on a rim joist ends there in its clean butt end or turns its whole end.
# ROUND 7 (kit §12.3, the walkway ruling: a bad-condition floor is decayed ALL OVER, then broken): above `age` 1 every
# board takes TimberKit's `Decay` (`decay` -1: none up to age 1, full at age 1.8; each board x (1 +- dstate)): ridges
# along the grain, open checks and an end split, crumbled ends, a sliver, a missing corner, thinner (sunk), narrower
# (wider, uneven gaps); each bay sags `bsag` between its joists; a few whole boards spring an end (`plift`, `liftc`);
# one whole board is gone two lanes or more from the hole (`missing`). Every board is uneven in every sense: widths
# 1.5:1 or more across the deck from age 1 (`wjit`; the lanes' layout grows to age 1 and then holds, so every state of
# one size has the same lanes), each lane's ends at the module's ends at their own inset and slant (`eivar`), twist,
# taper, a waney edge, thickness along, pitch and roll (`btwist` .. `broll`). A survivor across the hole stays straight
# on its joists and cracks underneath mid-bay, sagging `ssag` stiffly (no ribbon).
# ROUND 8 (the lead's look at round 7; kit §12.3: decayed all over, hard not soft, uneven in every sense): the planks are
# 2.6 cm (`board_t`; 1.9 read thin and papery); a decayed end rots back HARD (`EndRot`: three blocks across the width,
# each its own depth, the top layer stepped back further: never a wavy sheet or a dome); the JOISTS are old too
# (`JoistBlank`, decayed `jdecay` x the age: open checks with sharp walls along the sides and from an end, the grain
# eroded into ridges, the ends off square, breakouts on the bottom arrises), the snapped joist's halves
# included; a survivor across the hole is cracked THROUGH (`sthru`: a torn pair, short teeth across its top) with its
# two halves straight and kinked sharply (`sease`), never a bent ribbon; the debris SETTLES (G31 `collide=settle`):
# each fallen piece is dropped from over where it was, pulled `heap` toward the hole's middle (Wreck: the V), and rests
# on the ground, the Wreck's members that reach it and the pieces already down: a heap, not a tray of tiles.
# THE HOLE (rounds 2-5), calibrated to real broken floors (`Docs/Research/real-broken-floors.md`).
#
# Deck's knobs (also DeckDebris's; Wreck's are listed above `Wreck`):
#   knob        default   range          unit      meaning
#   size_x      200.0     100-400        cm        the module across the boards (lanes are added or dropped; the pitch stays)
#   size_y      200.0     100-400        cm        the module along the boards (the joists respace: size_y / joists)
#   damage      1.0       0-1.6                    how broken: the hole is damage x (hole_rx, hole_ry); 0 the intact floor, 1 the default, 1.6 the most
#   age         1.0       0-2                      how worn, the kit one age scale: every imperfection of the boards and joists x min(age, 1) + 2 max(age - 1, 0) (0 new and true, 1 aged, 2 three times the aged ranges); past 1.1 every board decays, fully at 1.8
#   noise       1         -              seed      the hole's seed: where it falls, every break, every fate
#   budget      1         0-2                      0 game (arrises chamfered, their round baked), 1 high (worn rounds), 2 ultra (8 segments, finer breaks)
#   softness    0.0       0-1            0-1       0 crisp, the default (owner: hard, not soft; arrises worn up to 6 mm, planar cup, jagged outlines, V checks, stepped ends); 1 worn round, driftwood-like (TimberKit's softv, forwarded to every board and joist)
#   board_w     14.0      8-40           cm        the boards' nominal width: the lanes' pitch
#   board_t     2.6       1.2-16         cm        the boards' thickness (round 8: 2.6, an old platform's planks)
#   board_gap   0.3       0.1-1          cm        the nominal gap the pitch allows for
#   joists      5         3-8            count     joists under the module
#   joist_w     3.8       3-30           cm        the joists' width
#   joist_d     18.4      10-30          cm        the joists' depth
#   fseed       5         -              seed      the floor's seed: lanes, joints, every board's draws; every state shares it, so a broken state swaps in
#   wjit        0.15      0-0.25         x pitch   each boundary between lanes moves up to this either way (lane widths +-2 wjit; grows to age 1, then holds, so every state has one layout)
#   gapmin      0.1       0-1            cm        the narrowest gap between two lanes
#   gapmax      0.8       0-2            cm        the widest gap between two lanes (at age 1)
#   egap        0.3       0-1            cm        the gap at the module's sides (half each side, so modules tile)
#   einset      0.05      0.02-40        cm        the boards' ends in from the module's ends
#   eivar       0.6       0-20           cm        each lane's ends a further 0-this in from the module's ends (x the age spread), each at its own slant
#   pnone       0.2       0-1            share     the lanes with no butt joint
#   ptwo        0.35      0-1            share     the jointed lanes with a second joint two joists on
#   bgmin       0.15      0.05-1         cm        the narrowest butt joint
#   bgmax       0.4       0.05-2         cm        the widest butt joint
#   bvar        0.015     0-0.05         x width   a board narrower than its lane by up to this
#   tvar        0.05      0-0.45         x thick   each board thicker or thinner by up to this
#   yaw         0.5       0-1.5          deg       each board turned 0.4-1 x this, held inside the gaps round it
#   lift        0.15      0-2            cm        each board raised by up to this (never sunk into its joists)
#   cup         0.3       0-3            cm        each board's edges this far off its middle (up on 3 boards of 4)
#   bow         0.25      0-1            cm        each board's middle raised up to this between its nails
#   crook       0.25      0-1            cm        each board's middle sideways up to this
#   endsq       1.5       0-5            deg       each butt joint up to this off square (both boards follow it)
#   wear        0.5       0-1.5          cm        the worn top arrises' mean radius (x 0.3 + 0.7 age)
#   wearvar     0.6       0-1            x wear    how much the radius varies, board to board and along a board
#   jvw         0.05      0-0.15         x         each joist's width +- this
#   jvd         0.03      0-0.1          x         each joist's depth +- this
#   jsag        0.4       0-2            cm        each joist sags 0.4-1 x this
#   jcrook      0.3       0-1            cm        each joist crooked sideways up to this
#   jdecay      1.0       0-1            x         round 8: how old the joists look (budget 1-2): x min(age, 1) x (0.35 + 0.65 of the way from age 1 to 1.8); checks, eroded grain, ends off square, breakouts
#   jcheck      0.35      0-0.45         x width   a joist's side check this deep at full decay (its end check 1.25 x)
#   jends       0.6       0-0.6          cm        a joist's ends off square up to this, through the depth and across the width
#   ties        0         0-3            count     round 8 (R3): old squared cross timbers under the joists, across the module (along Y), their ends out past the plank ends
#   tie_w       14.0      6-30           cm        a cross timber's width and depth
#   tiep        1.0       0-1            share     round 11: the share of modules with a support (the lashed cross timbers at one end, where the stringers meet)
#   tieat       3         0-3            choice    round 12: where the support sits: 0 the module's start (x = 0; modules end to end are a support at every joint), 1 its end, 2 both (the last module of a run, always present), 3 an end drawn from the floor seed
#   rope        0         0-1            flag      round 9-10 (R3): round rope turns lashed round each cross timber near both its ends (slot `Rope`)
#   ropes       3         1-5            count     round 10: the rope turns at each end of a cross timber
#   grit        0         0-60           count     round 9 (R3): small stones 1-3 cm scattered over the deck and settled (G31), besides `stones`
#   stones      0         0-20           count     round 8-9 (R3): stones lying on the deck, each dropped on its own place (a share drifting toward one side) and settled (G31); slot `Stone`
#   stonesz     7.0       2-20           cm        the stones' mean size (0.45-1.45 x)
#   stonesc     0         0-20           count     round 10 (R3): stones in one loose cluster (within 18 cm of a drawn spot over a plank), besides the singles
#   shade       0.15      0-0.6          x         each board's state: darkened by up to this (x the age spread) in vertex colour R
#   btwist      0.5       0-6            deg       each board's ends turned against each other up to this (AgedBoard `twist`)
#   btaper      0.03      0-0.2          x         each board narrower at one end by up to this (held inside its lane)
#   bwaney      0.0       0-1.5          cm        one edge of each board wavy (a waney edge), inward up to twice this (0 by default: the owner's straight outlines)
#   bttaper     0.04      0-0.3          x         each board thinner at one end by up to this
#   bpitch      0.15      0-3            deg       each board's ends up and down by up to this (the board lifted so its low end rests)
#   broll       0.3       0-8            deg       each board rolled about its length (one edge proud) up to this
#   decay       -1.0      -1-1           0-1       -1: from age (none up to age 1.1, full at age 1.8, as AgedBoard); else how decayed every board is (AgedBoard's `Decay`)
#   dstate      0.35      0-1            x         each board's decay x (1 +- this): one fresher, one more rotten
#   ridge       0.45      0-2            cm        decay: each board's top eroded to ridges along the grain, this deep
#   groove      0.0       0-3            cm        round 8 (R3): crisp V grooves along the grain sunk this deep (x the decay) into a share of each top's columns, long and fading; 0 none
#   gshare      0.35      0-1            share     the share of a top's columns that carry a groove
#   gouge       0.0       0-4            cm        round 9 (R3): 2-4 long irregular V gouges a plank top, this deep at most (x the decay), each its own place, wander, length and width; 0 none
#   lips        0.0       0-3            cm        round 9: the top arrises broken off in irregular runs along both edges, this deep (x the decay)
#   hollow      0.0       0-2            cm        round 9: one shallow worn hollow a plank, this deep (x the decay)
#   edgew       0.0       0-3            cm        round 10 (R3): both long edges wander in up to this (x the decay), in long waves and broken runs; 0 straight
#   checks      3         0-3            count     decay: open checks and splits along the grain, up to this many a board
#   checkd      0.45      0-0.9          x thick   decay: a check this deep (an end split deeper)
#   crumb       4.0       0-20           cm        decay: each board's ends rounded and crumbled back up to this
#   sliver      0.6       0-1            share     decay: boards with a sliver split off an edge
#   corner      0.45      0-1            share     decay: boards with a corner missing
#   thin        0.15      0-0.6          x         decay: boards thinner by up to this (worn and sunk)
#   shrink      0.06      0-0.3          x         decay: boards narrower by up to this (wider, uneven gaps)
#   bsag        0.8       0-4            cm        decay: each board sags this between its joists (x its decay)
#   plift       0.08      0-1            share     decay: whole boards with one end sprung up (x the decay)
#   liftc       2.5       0-10           cm        a sprung end's lift
#   missing     1         0-1            flag      decay: one whole board gone, two lanes or more clear of the hole (above half decay)
#   missp       1.0       0-1            share     round 12: the share of modules (by the floor seed) where `missing` takes a board
#   tiein       0.0       0-1            share     round 13: the supports' ends sit back under the planks (0.6-1.5 x `einset` x this, each end its own); 0 the full width
#   tiex        0.0       0-40           cm        round 13: each support drifts up to this far in from its module end, so a run's supports are not evenly spaced
#   hole_x      0.5       0-1            x size_x  the hole's centre across the boards, a share of the module
#   hole_y      0.5       0-1            x size_y  the hole's centre along the boards, a share of the module
#   hole_rx     55.0      5-150          cm        the half-span across the boards at damage 1 (Wreck: the collapse's)
#   hole_ry     35.0      5-100          cm        the half-length along the boards at damage 1
#   cvar        25.0      0-50           cm        each seed moves the centre up to this
#   svar        0.25      0-0.5          x         each seed scales the span and length by up to this
#   jump        0.1       0-1            share     of the boards, where a rim steps a bay to the next joist
#   midbay      0.42      0-1            share     of the level and cracked ends, those 5-15 cm off their joist
#   pshort      0.4       0-1            share     of those, the ones short of the joist (the joist left bare)
#   gmin        18.0      5-60           cm        the least board removed between a board's two ends
#   survive     2         0-2            count     the most boards that survive across the hole (each seed draws 0 to this)
#   ssag        2.5       0-6            cm        a survivor's sag at its crack (0.5-1 x), its halves straight
#   sthru       1         0-1            flag      round 8: the survivor cracked THROUGH (a torn pair, short teeth across its top); 0 cracked underneath only (round 7)
#   sease       0.05      0.02-0.3       x         how much of each half bends into the kink (0.05 a sharp kink; 0.3 round 7's ease, which read as a ribbon)
#   plevel      0.6       0-1            share     ends left level
#   phang       0.25      0-1            share     ends hanging hlo-hhi
#   pcrack      0.1       0-1            share     ends cracked and sagging clo-chi (the rest are steep)
#   hlo         15.0      0-80           deg       a hanging end's least turn
#   hhi         45.0      0-85           deg       a hanging end's most turn
#   clo         5.0       0-40           deg       a cracked end's least turn
#   chi         15.0      0-45           deg       a cracked end's most turn
#   slo         60.0      30-85          deg       a steep end's least turn
#   shi         80.0      30-88          deg       a steep end's most turn
#   stub        1         0-1            flag      one board near an end of the span hangs a stub from one nail
#   nmin        10.0      4-30           cm        the stub's least length
#   nmax        15.0      4-30           cm        the stub's most length
#   nlo         35.0      10-80          deg       the stub's least turn
#   nhi         45.0      10-85          deg       the stub's most turn
#   rimfrag     1         0-1            flag      a loose torn piece lying on one rim's boards
#   rimchips    4         0-10           count     chips beside it
#   long        0.5       0-1            share     breaks that are long (splintered) rather than short
#   deep        0.75      0.2-1.5        x width   a short break's spire depth
#   ldeep       1.3       0.4-2.5        x width   a long break's spire depth
#   splint      1.0       0.2-2          x         the long-splinter scale
#   slant       12.0      0-20           deg       each break's slant, either way (Damage's limit is about 20)
#   grain       0.24      0.1-0.6        x width   a break's spire width
#   lean        1.6       0-3            x thick   how far a break's top face tears from its bottom
#   horn        0.3       0-1            share     breaks with one horn
#   rings       0         0-1            flag      Damage's partition: 0 rows x columns, 1 rings x rays
#   torn        0.85      0-1                      round 9's blunt torn ends on short breaks
#   torntilt    0.15      0-0.5                    how far each torn end tilts
#   tornrib     1         0-1            flag      one ribbon length per bundle
#   tornsep     0.15      0-0.5                    how deep the cracks between bundles run
#   uvbox       1         0-1            flag      each piece mapped by one box after its breaks
#   detail      0.14      0.06-0.4       cm        a board break's point spacing (under 0.06 Damage's chew refuses)
#   hdetail     0.12      0.06-0.4       cm        a hinge's or a survivor crack's point spacing
#   jdetail     0.3       0.1-0.6        cm        a snapped joist's point spacing
#   tile        100.0     20-400         cm        one UV tile
#   aspect      1.0       0.25-4                   along-grain tile over across
#
# DeckDebris adds:
#   knob        default   range          unit      meaning
#   dmin        10.0      4-60           cm        a removed run shorter than this is lost (WreckDebris: lies as crumbs)
#   dshort      0.0       0-120          cm        a fragment shorter than this takes plain fresh ends
#   frag        80.0      30-200         cm        the fragments' mean length
#   grow        1.3       1-2.5          x         the pile's footprint over the hole's
#   tumble      8.0       0-45           deg       each fragment tumbled up to this
#   tilt        0.35      0-1            share     fragments lying tilted, one end raised
#   edge        0.12      0-1            share     fragments lying on edge
#   lsplit      0.3       0-1            share     fragments split along their length
#   splinters   0.3       0-1            share     boards that leave a loose splinter
#   ddetail     0.07      0.06-0.3       cm        the fragments' point spacing
#   heap        0.45      0-0.9          share     round 8: each fragment dropped from over where it was, pulled this share toward the hole's middle, then settled (G31)
#
# THE COLLAPSE (`Wreck`, `SM_WoodDeck_Wrecked`): see its own header below.
#
# THE DEBRIS (`DeckDebris`): what the hole lost, on its own ground plane (z = 0 is the floor below; place it at the
# module's X/Y; its build line takes a 20 cm margin round the module, kit 2.0.3). Each lane's removed run of `dmin` cm
# or more becomes 1-3 aged fragments whose ends are the rim's own breaks, tooth into socket (a butt end sawn), and
# fresh breaks between them, each dropped from over where it lay and SETTLED (round 8, G31) into a heap on the ground
# and the pieces before it (`heap`); `grow` sizes the ground the small pieces scatter on. Game tier only.
#
# BUILD LINES: every state is a line below; build only the lines you need (a whole build is many minutes: the broken
# and wrecked `_Ultra` lines are the slow ones). The WEATHERED walkway (round 8-10, copied from the owner's R3) is
# `SM_WoodDeck_Weathered` (game, maps baked from its High) and `SM_WoodDeck_Weathered_High`, 200 x 300 cm.
# BUDGET TIERS (kit §12.1, §8a item 6): one recipe, the knob `budget`. Each state's `SM_WoodDeck_<State>` is the light
# game tier, `[triangles=N, maps=(normal, ao), from=$<State>High]` (budget 0: arrises chamfered, their round and the
# fine break baked); `SM_WoodDeck_<State>_High` (budget 1) and `_Ultra` (budget 2: 8 segments along a board; its
# wrapper also passes every break's point spacing 0.6 x) the full-detail grades; their size is the author's choice.

build {
  SM_WoodDeck_Intact            = $DeckIntactGame [bounds=(200, 200, *), pivot=(0, 0, 0), triangles=2000, maps=(normal, ao), from=$DeckIntactHigh, resolution=1024, supersample=1]
  SM_WoodDeck_Intact_High       = $DeckIntactHigh [bounds=(200, 200, *), pivot=(0, 0, 0)]
  SM_WoodDeck_Intact_Ultra      = $DeckIntactUltra [bounds=(200, 200, *), pivot=(0, 0, 0)]
  SM_WoodDeck_Weathered         = $DeckWeatheredGame [bounds=(200, 300, *), pivot=(0, 0, 0), triangles=6000, maps=(normal, ao), from=$DeckWeatheredHigh, resolution=1024, supersample=1]
  SM_WoodDeck_Weathered_High    = $DeckWeatheredHigh [bounds=(200, 300, *), pivot=(0, 0, 0), triangles=40000]
  SM_WoodDeck_Broken            = $DeckBrokenGame [bounds=(200, 200, *), pivot=(0, 0, 0), triangles=9000, maps=(normal, ao), from=$DeckBrokenHigh, resolution=1024, supersample=1]
  SM_WoodDeck_Broken_High       = $DeckBrokenHigh [bounds=(200, 200, *), pivot=(0, 0, 0)]
  SM_WoodDeck_Broken_Ultra      = $DeckBrokenUltra [bounds=(200, 200, *), pivot=(0, 0, 0)]
  SM_WoodDeck_Wrecked           = $DeckWreckedGame [bounds=(200, 200, *), pivot=(0, 0, 0), triangles=12000, maps=(normal, ao), from=$DeckWreckedHigh, resolution=1024, supersample=1]
  SM_WoodDeck_Wrecked_High      = $DeckWreckedHigh [bounds=(200, 200, *), pivot=(0, 0, 0)]
  SM_WoodDeck_Wrecked_Ultra     = $DeckWreckedUltra [bounds=(200, 200, *), pivot=(0, 0, 0)]
  SM_WoodDeck_Broken_300        = $DeckBroken300Game [bounds=(300, 200, *), pivot=(0, 0, 0), triangles=10000, maps=(normal, ao), from=$DeckBroken300High, resolution=1024, supersample=1]
  SM_WoodDeck_Broken_300_High   = $DeckBroken300High [bounds=(300, 200, *), pivot=(0, 0, 0)]
  SM_WoodDeck_Broken_300_Ultra  = $DeckBroken300Ultra [bounds=(300, 200, *), pivot=(0, 0, 0)]
  SM_WoodDeck_Broken_Debris     = $DeckBrokenDebris [bounds=(240, 240, *), pivot=(0, 0, 0), triangles=10000]
  SM_WoodDeck_Wrecked_Debris    = $DeckWreckedDebris [bounds=(240, 240, *), pivot=(0, 0, 0), triangles=12000]
  SM_WoodDeck_Broken_300_Debris = $DeckBroken300Debris [bounds=(340, 240, *), pivot=(0, 0, 0), triangles=10000]
}

Face   = material()
Broken = material()
Nail   = material()
Block  = material()
Stone  = material()
Dmg    = shape('/GraphCodeShape/Presets/Damage')
Debris = shape('/GraphCodeShape/Presets/Debris', Face = $Face, Broken = $Broken)
Rope   = material()
Kit    = shape('/GraphCodeShape/Presets/TimberKit', Face = $Face, Broken = $Broken, Rope = $Rope, Stone = $Stone, Iron = $Nail)
CP     = shape('/GraphCodeShape/Presets/ConcreteParts', Face = $Stone, Broken = $Stone)

# the generator hash, written once (kit G28 named formula): the fraction of a sine of a seed and a constant
Hash = formula(s, c) { sin($s * 12.9898 + $c) * 43758.5453 - floor(sin($s * 12.9898 + $c) * 43758.5453) }
# the wear of the boards, from the knob, the age factor and the softness
WearMix = formula(w, f, s) { min($w * (0.3 + 0.7 * $f), 0.6) + $s * (1.75 - min($w * (0.3 + 0.7 * $f), 0.6)) }

# ---- blanks ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# a plain board in the Damage frame: centred on x, bottom on z = 0, y from 0 to length; its grain +Y (the snapped
# joist's halves are built from it)
Plank = mesh(width=14.0, thick=1.9, length=200.0, tile=100.0, aspect=1.0) {
  rect(w=$width, h=$length)
  extrude(height=$thick)
  place(by=(0.0, 0.5 * $length, 0.0))
  uv(box, facing=(0, 0, 1), up=(0, 1, 0), scale=($aspect * $tile, $tile, $tile))
  material($Face)
}

# a straight path along +Y, 0 to 100 cm in 41 stations: a board swept along it has rings to bend
Run100 = plane() { points((0.0, 0.0, 0.0), (0.0, 2.5, 0.0), (0.0, 5.0, 0.0), (0.0, 7.5, 0.0), (0.0, 10.0, 0.0), (0.0, 12.5, 0.0), (0.0, 15.0, 0.0), (0.0, 17.5, 0.0), (0.0, 20.0, 0.0), (0.0, 22.5, 0.0), (0.0, 25.0, 0.0), (0.0, 27.5, 0.0), (0.0, 30.0, 0.0), (0.0, 32.5, 0.0), (0.0, 35.0, 0.0), (0.0, 37.5, 0.0), (0.0, 40.0, 0.0), (0.0, 42.5, 0.0), (0.0, 45.0, 0.0), (0.0, 47.5, 0.0), (0.0, 50.0, 0.0), (0.0, 52.5, 0.0), (0.0, 55.0, 0.0), (0.0, 57.5, 0.0), (0.0, 60.0, 0.0), (0.0, 62.5, 0.0), (0.0, 65.0, 0.0), (0.0, 67.5, 0.0), (0.0, 70.0, 0.0), (0.0, 72.5, 0.0), (0.0, 75.0, 0.0), (0.0, 77.5, 0.0), (0.0, 80.0, 0.0), (0.0, 82.5, 0.0), (0.0, 85.0, 0.0), (0.0, 87.5, 0.0), (0.0, 90.0, 0.0), (0.0, 92.5, 0.0), (0.0, 95.0, 0.0), (0.0, 97.5, 0.0), (0.0, 100.0, 0.0)) }

# the ground a debris pile falls on (scaled to the hole's footprint), deleted again by its handle
Disc = mesh() {
  circle(radius=1.0, segments=32)
  extrude(height=1.0)
}

# the floor under a settling pile (round 8, G31 `obstacle=`): any piece that tips off the heap rests on it; never drawn
PileFloor = mesh() {
  rect(w=1200.0, h=1200.0)
  extrude(height=4.0)
  place(by=(0.0, 0.0, -4.0))
}

# TimberKit's worn section (`AgedSec3`'s outline, read from its generator) swept along 40 stations: a board that bends
AgedRing = mesh(w=20.0, t=5.0, a=0.5, b=0.5, c=0.15, d=0.15) {
  points((-0.5 * $w + $d, 0.0), (0.0, 0.0), (0.5 * $w - $c, 0.0), (0.5 * $w, 0.364 * $c), (0.5 * $w, $t - $b), (0.5 * $w - 0.234 * $b, $t - 0.3572 * $b), (0.5 * $w - 0.3572 * $b, $t - 0.234 * $b), (0.5 * $w - $b, $t), (0.0, $t), (-0.5 * $w + $a, $t), (-0.5 * $w + 0.3572 * $a, $t - 0.234 * $a), (-0.5 * $w + 0.234 * $a, $t - 0.3572 * $a), (-0.5 * $w, $t - $a), (-0.5 * $w, 0.364 * $d), loop=true)
  sweep(along=$Run100)
}
# and its decayed section (`DecaySec`'s outline, 19 columns across the top) on the same 40 stations
DecayRing = mesh(w=20.0, t=5.0, a=0.5, b=0.5, c=0.15, d=0.15) {
  points((-0.5 * $w + $d, 0.0), (0.0, 0.0), (0.5 * $w - $c, 0.0), (0.5 * $w, 0.364 * $c), (0.5 * $w, 0.5 * $t), (0.5 * $w, $t - $b), (0.5 * $w - $b - 0 * ($w - $a - $b) / 18, $t), (0.5 * $w - $b - 1 * ($w - $a - $b) / 18, $t), (0.5 * $w - $b - 2 * ($w - $a - $b) / 18, $t), (0.5 * $w - $b - 3 * ($w - $a - $b) / 18, $t), (0.5 * $w - $b - 4 * ($w - $a - $b) / 18, $t), (0.5 * $w - $b - 5 * ($w - $a - $b) / 18, $t), (0.5 * $w - $b - 6 * ($w - $a - $b) / 18, $t), (0.5 * $w - $b - 7 * ($w - $a - $b) / 18, $t), (0.5 * $w - $b - 8 * ($w - $a - $b) / 18, $t), (0.5 * $w - $b - 9 * ($w - $a - $b) / 18, $t), (0.5 * $w - $b - 10 * ($w - $a - $b) / 18, $t), (0.5 * $w - $b - 11 * ($w - $a - $b) / 18, $t), (0.5 * $w - $b - 12 * ($w - $a - $b) / 18, $t), (0.5 * $w - $b - 13 * ($w - $a - $b) / 18, $t), (0.5 * $w - $b - 14 * ($w - $a - $b) / 18, $t), (0.5 * $w - $b - 15 * ($w - $a - $b) / 18, $t), (0.5 * $w - $b - 16 * ($w - $a - $b) / 18, $t), (0.5 * $w - $b - 17 * ($w - $a - $b) / 18, $t), (0.5 * $w - $b - 18 * ($w - $a - $b) / 18, $t), (-0.5 * $w, $t - $a), (-0.5 * $w, 0.5 * $t), (-0.5 * $w, 0.364 * $d), loop=true)
  sweep(along=$Run100)
}

# ONE BOARD OF A LANE THAT SAGS (an aged board, decayed as `DeckBoard`, on 40 stations), placed at y = a0 in the
# module's frame along the board: STIFF, cracked UNDERNEATH at y = yc (`crack` 1 on the board over it: a torn pair,
# `side` 1 the -Y half, -1 the +Y half), each half a straight line from its support hl back down to vd at the crack:
# z = -vq (v^2 - max(v - ease, 0)^2) / (2 ease) with v = 1 at the crack, 0 at the support (round 7: the Broken
# state's survivor, cracked mid-bay over the hole, `tx` degrees more twist; the Wrecked state's boards over a
# shallow V). No ribbon: a board this thin snaps or sags a few cm stiffly.
BentBoard = mesh(width=14.0, thick=1.9, length=200.0, wvar=0.015, tvar=0.05, lvar=0.0, yaw=0.5, lift=0.15, cup=0.3, bow=0.25, crook=0.25, endsq=1.5, wear=0.5, wearvar=0.6, arris=3, seg=4, room=0.2, g0=0.1, ea0=0.0, g1=0.1, ea1=0.0, a0=0.0, crack=0, side=1, yc=100.0, hl=18.0, vd=2.0, ease=0.3, tx=0.0, thru=0, hdetail=0.12, nc=1, shade=0.0, tile=100.0, aspect=1.0, softness=0.0, twist=0.0, taper=0.0, waney=0.0, ttaper=0.0, pitch=0.0, roll=0.0, decay=0.0, state=0.35, ridge=0.45, checks=3, checkd=0.45, crumb=4.0, sliver=0.6, corner=0.45, thin=0.15, shrink=0.06, bsag=0.0, js=40.0, sy=200.0, ys=0.0, noise=1, index=0, groove=0.0, gshare=0.35, gouge=0.0, lips=0.0, hollow=0.0, edgew=0.0) {
  $K = $noise * 1009 + $index
  $Uo = $Hash($K, 7311.3)
  $Vo = $Hash($K, 7337.9)
  $Uf = 2 * floor(2 * $Hash($K, 7363.1)) - 1
  loop (20) {
    $ix = output.index
    $ad[$ix] = $Hash($K, floor(10 * (3.1 + 17.3 * $ix) + 0.5) / 10)
  }
  $Wd = $width * (1 + $wvar * (2 * $ad[1] - 1))
  $Td = $thick * (1 + $tvar * (2 * $ad[2] - 1))
  $Ld = $length * (1 + $lvar * (2 * $ad[3] - 1))
  $yw = $yaw * (0.4 + 0.6 * $ad[4]) * (2 * floor(2 * $ad[5]) - 1)
  $lf = $lift * (2 * $ad[6] - 1)
  $cp = $cup * (0.3 + 0.7 * $ad[7]) * (1 - 2 * clamp(ceil($ad[8] - 0.75), 0, 1))
  $bw = $bow * (2 * $ad[9] - 1)
  $ck = $crook * (2 * $ad[10] - 1)
  $e0 = $endsq * (2 * $ad[11] - 1)
  $e1 = $endsq * (2 * $ad[12] - 1)
  $rcap = min(0.3 * $Wd, 0.4 * $Td)
  $ra = min(max($wear * (1 + $wearvar * (2 * $ad[13] - 1)), 0.1 * $wear), $rcap)
  $rb = min(max($wear * (1 + $wearvar * (2 * $ad[14] - 1)), 0.1 * $wear), $rcap)
  $rc = min(0.35 * $wear * (0.6 + 0.8 * $ad[15]), $rcap)
  $rd = min(0.35 * $wear * (0.6 + 0.8 * $ad[16]), $rcap)
  $rm = max($ra, $rb)
  $wa = min($wearvar, 0.8) * (0.3 + 0.7 * $ad[17])
  $wb = min($wearvar, 0.8) * (0.3 + 0.7 * $ad[18])
  $ph = 360 * $ad[19]
  $fr = 0.6 + 1.2 * $ad[20]
  loop (24) {
    $ix = output.index + 20
    $ad[$ix] = $Hash($K, floor(10 * (3.1 + 17.3 * $ix) + 0.5) / 10)
  }
  $tw = $twist * (0.3 + 0.7 * $ad[21]) * (2 * floor(2 * $ad[22]) - 1)
  $tp = $taper * (2 * $ad[23] - 1)
  $wv = $waney * (0.3 + 0.7 * $ad[24])
  $wk = 0.5 + 1.5 * $ad[25]
  $ws = 2 * floor(2 * $ad[26]) - 1
  $tt = $ttaper * (2 * $ad[27] - 1)
  $pt = $pitch * (2 * $ad[28] - 1)
  $rl = $roll * (2 * $ad[29] - 1)
  $dv = clamp($decay * (1 + $state * (2 * $ad[30] - 1)), 0, 1)
  $nck = min(floor($checks * (0.4 + 0.6 * $ad[31]) + 0.5), 3) * clamp(ceil($dv - 0.05), 0, 1)
  $cx1 = 3 + floor(13 * $ad[32])
  $cx2 = 3 + floor(13 * $ad[33])
  $cx3 = 3 + floor(13 * $ad[34])
  $cy1 = 0.05 + 0.3 * $ad[35]
  $cl1 = 0.3 + 0.6 * $ad[36]
  $cy2 = 0.35 + 0.4 * $ad[37]
  $cl2 = 1.0
  $cy3 = 0.0
  $cl3 = 0.15 + 0.4 * $ad[38]
  $sl = clamp(ceil($sliver * $dv - $ad[39]), 0, 1)
  $sly = 0.1 + 0.5 * $ad[40]
  $co = clamp(ceil($corner * $dv - $ad[41]), 0, 1)
  $coe = floor(2 * $ad[42])
  $cos = 2 * floor(2 * $ad[43]) - 1
  $crf = 0.5 + 0.5 * $ad[44]
  $Wd0 = max($Wd, 11.0)
  $Td0 = $Td
  $Wd = ($Wd - 2 * $wv) * (1 - 0.5 * abs($tp)) * (1 - $shrink * $dv)
  $Td = $Td * (1 - $thin * $dv)
  $tw = $tw + $tx * (2 * floor(2 * $ad[22]) - 1)
  $lf = abs($lf) + max(-$cp, 0) + 0.5 * $Ld * abs(tan($pt)) + 0.5 * $Wd * abs(sin($rl)) + 0.5 * $Wd * abs(sin(0.5 * $tw))
  $bw = abs($bw)
  $e0 = $ea0
  $e1 = $ea1
  $kq = min(1, $room / max(0.5 * $Ld * abs(sin($yw)) + abs($ck), 0.001), max(min($g0, $g1) - 0.01, 0) / max(0.5 * $Wd * abs(sin($yw)), 0.0001))
  $yw = $yw * $kq
  $ck = $ck * $kq
  $cu = 0.0
  $cf = 0.5
  $cs = 0
  if ($dv > 0.001) {
    add($DecayRing, w=$Wd, t=$Td, a=max($ra, 0.25), b=max($rb, 0.25), c=$rc, d=$rd, scale=(1.0, $Ld / 100.0, 1.0))
    $NC = 18
  } else {
    add($AgedRing, w=$Wd, t=$Td, a=$ra, b=$rb, c=$rc, d=$rd, scale=(1.0, $Ld / 100.0, 1.0))
  }
  if ($crack > 0.5) {
    if ($thru > 0.5) {
      # round 8: cracked THROUGH (the lead: "one board over the hole still reads as a smooth bent ribbon"): a torn
      # pair with short teeth across the top, the two halves straight and kinked sharply at it
      if ($side > 0) {
        $Dmg.Snap(width=$Wd0, thick=$Td0, deep=0.38, grain=0.3, lean=1.0, layers=2, uneven=0.4, rough=1.0, long=0.5, vdep=0.6, torn=0.85, torntilt=0.15, tornrib=1, tornsep=0.15, loss=0.0, chew=0.05, detail=$hdetail, noise=$nc, origin=(0.0, $yc - $a0, 0.0), uvfit=0, tile=$tile, aspect=$aspect)
      } else {
        $Dmg.SnapOff(width=$Wd0, thick=$Td0, deep=0.38, grain=0.3, lean=1.0, layers=2, uneven=0.4, rough=1.0, long=0.5, vdep=0.6, torn=0.85, torntilt=0.15, tornrib=1, tornsep=0.15, loss=0.0, chew=0.05, detail=$hdetail, noise=$nc, origin=(0.0, $yc - $a0, 0.0), uvfit=0, tile=$tile, aspect=$aspect)
      }
    } else {
      if ($side > 0) {
        $Dmg.Snap(width=$Wd0, thick=$Td0, deep=0.0, lean=0.6, wander=0.05, layers=2, fray=0.0, loss=0.0, chew=0.0, thin=0.0, detail=$hdetail, noise=$nc, origin=(0.0, $yc - $a0, 0.0), uvfit=0, tile=$tile, aspect=$aspect)
      } else {
        $Dmg.SnapOff(width=$Wd0, thick=$Td0, deep=0.0, lean=0.6, wander=0.05, layers=2, fray=0.0, loss=0.0, chew=0.0, thin=0.0, detail=$hdetail, noise=$nc, origin=(0.0, $yc - $a0, 0.0), uvfit=0, tile=$tile, aspect=$aspect)
      }
    }
    keep(largest)
  }
  if ($dv > 0.001) {
    $Kit.Decay(w=$Wd, t=$Td, len=$Ld, a=max($ra, 0.25), b=max($rb, 0.25), dv=$dv, ridge=$ridge, ph=$ph, cd1=clamp(ceil($nck - 0.5), 0, 1) * $checkd * $Td * $dv, cd2=clamp(ceil($nck - 1.5), 0, 1) * $checkd * $Td * $dv, cd3=clamp(ceil($nck - 2.5), 0, 1) * min(1.6 * $checkd, 0.85) * $Td * $dv, cx1=$cx1, cx2=$cx2, cx3=$cx3, cy1=$cy1, cl1=$cl1, cy2=$cy2, cl2=$cl2, cy3=$cy3, cl3=$cl3, crumb=$crumb * $dv * $softness, crf=$crf, sl=$sl, sly=$sly, co=$co, coe=$coe, cos=$cos, nc=$NC, softv=$softness)
    if ($groove * $dv > 0.001) {
      $Kit.Grooves(w=$Wd, t=$Td, a=max($ra, 0.25), b=max($rb, 0.25), nc=$NC, dv=$dv, gd=$groove, gs=$gshare, ph=$ph)
    }
    if (($gouge + $lips + $hollow + $edgew) * $dv > 0.001) {
      $Kit.Gouges(w=$Wd, t=$Td, len=$Ld, a=max($ra, 0.25), b=max($rb, 0.25), nc=$NC, dv=$dv, gd=$gouge, lp=$lips, hd=$hollow, ew=$edgew, k=$K + 17)
    }
    $er1 = $Hash($K, 6101.3)
    $er2 = $Hash($K, 6133.1)
    $er3 = $Hash($K, 6167.9)
    $er4 = $Hash($K, 6199.7)
    $er5 = $Hash($K, 6231.3)
    $er6 = $Hash($K, 6263.9)
    $er7 = $Hash($K, 6295.1)
    $er8 = $Hash($K, 6329.7)
    $Kit.EndRot(w=$Wd, t=$Td, len=$Ld, r0=$crumb * $dv * $crf * (1 - $softness), r1=$crumb * $dv * (1 - $softness), b1=$Wd * (0.12 + 0.2 * $er1 - 0.5), b2=$Wd * (0.55 + 0.25 * $er2 - 0.5), h1=0.1 + 0.9 * $er3, h2=0.1 + 0.9 * $er4, h3=0.1 + 0.9 * $er5, h4=0.1 + 0.9 * $er6, h5=0.1 + 0.9 * $er7, h6=0.1 + 0.9 * $er8, lg=0.15 + 0.15 * $er1, ph=$ph)
  }
  $Kit.Age(w=$Wd, t=$Td, len=$Ld, cupv=$cp, bowv=$bw, crookv=$ck, e0=$e0, e1=$e1, yawv=$yw, liftv=$lf, rm=$rm * (1 - clamp(ceil($dv - 0.001), 0, 1)), wa=$wa, wb=$wb, ph=$ph, fr=$fr, twistv=$tw, taperv=$tp, wanev=$wv, wanek=$wk, wanes=$ws, ttapv=$tt, pitchv=$pt, rollv=$rl, curlv=$cu, curlf=$cf, curls=$cs, softv=$softness)
  place(by=(0.0, $a0, 0.0))
  $vq = $vd / (1 - 0.5 * $ease)
  $ka = $vq / ($ease * $hl)
  warp(by=(0.0, $side * (point.z - $Td) * $ka * min(clamp(1 - $side * ($yc - point.y) / $hl, 0, 1), $ease), -$vq * (clamp(1 - $side * ($yc - point.y) / $hl, 0, 1) * clamp(1 - $side * ($yc - point.y) / $hl, 0, 1) - max(clamp(1 - $side * ($yc - point.y) / $hl, 0, 1) - $ease, 0) * max(clamp(1 - $side * ($yc - point.y) / $hl, 0, 1) - $ease, 0)) / (2 * $ease)))
  if ($crack > 0.5) {
    uv(box, facing=(0, 0, 1), up=(0, $Uf, 0), scale=($aspect * $tile, $tile, $tile), offset=($Uo, $Vo)) [!cut]
    if (1 > 0.5) {
      uv(box, facing=(0, 0, 1), up=(0, $Uf, 0), scale=($aspect * $tile, $tile, $tile), offset=($Uo + 0.37, $Vo + 0.61)) [cut]
    }
    material($Face)
    material($Broken) [cut]
  } else {
    uv(box, facing=(0, 0, 1), up=(0, $Uf, 0), scale=($aspect * $tile, $tile, $tile), offset=($Uo, $Vo))
    material($Face)
  }
  $sh = $Hash($K, 4127.3)
  colour(1 - $shade * $sh, channel=r)
}

# half of a snapped joist in the Damage frame (grain +Y, depth up +Z): from its bearing (origin, bottom
# edge) to a `BeamBreak` at y = len (round 3: round 9's torn ends, as the deck passes them)
JoistEnd = mesh(len=100.0, w=3.8, d=18.4, detail=0.3, torn=0.0, torntilt=0.0, tornrib=0, tornsep=0.15, tile=100.0, aspect=1.0, noise=1, jdv=0.0, jcheck=0.35, jends=0.6, jchips=2) {
  if ($jdv > 0.001) {
    add($Kit.JoistBlank, w=$w, t=$d, len=$len + 30.0, dv=$jdv, checkd=$jcheck, ends=$jends, chips=$jchips, tile=$tile, aspect=$aspect, noise=$noise, index=7)
  } else {
    add($Plank, width=$w, thick=$d, length=$len + 30.0, tile=$tile, aspect=$aspect)
  }
  $Dmg.BeamBreak(width=$w, thick=$d, torn=$torn, torntilt=$torntilt, tornrib=$tornrib, tornsep=$tornsep, detail=$detail, noise=$noise, origin=(0.0, $len, 0.0), uvfit=0, tile=$tile, aspect=$aspect)
  keep(largest)
  material($Face)
  material($Broken) [cut]
}

# A FRAGMENT of a board (round 6: aged, the board's own section and wear), y from 0 to len: its -Y end the complement of
# the break `n0` (tooth into socket), its +Y end a fresh break `n1` or, `far` 1, the complement of the far rim's break,
# which was made turned 180 degrees; `saw0`/`saw1` 1 a sawn (butt) end instead; `split` 1 splits it along its length
# at `sx` of the width from its -X side and keeps the larger strip. q0/q1 are each break's lean (Damage's `lean`).
Frag = mesh(len=40.0, width=14.0, thick=1.9, wvar=0.015, tvar=0.05, lvar=0.0, yaw=0.0, lift=0.0, cup=0.3, bow=0.0, crook=0.0, endsq=0.0, wear=0.5, wearvar=0.6, arris=1, seg=1, length=40.0, noise=1, index=0, saw0=0, saw1=0, n0=1, l0=0.75, a0=0.0, r0=0.24, q0=1.6, s0=0.8, v0=0.7, h0=0.0, n1=2, l1=0.75, a1=0.0, r1=0.24, q1=1.6, s1=0.8, v1=0.7, h1=0.0, far=0, split=0, sx=0.5, tl=0.0, ed=0.0, detail=0.1, t0=0.0, t1=0.0, torntilt=0.0, tornrib=0, tornsep=0.15, tile=100.0, aspect=1.0, softness=0.0, twist=0.0, taper=0.0, waney=0.0, ttaper=0.0, pitch=0.0, roll=0.0, decay=0.0, state=0.35, ridge=0.45, checks=3, checkd=0.45, crumb=4.0, sliver=0.6, corner=0.45, thin=0.15, shrink=0.06, groove=0.0, gshare=0.35, gouge=0.0, lips=0.0, hollow=0.0, edgew=0.0) {
  $K = $noise * 1009 + $index
  $Uo = $Hash($K, 7311.3)
  $Vo = $Hash($K, 7337.9)
  $Uf = 2 * floor(2 * $Hash($K, 7363.1)) - 1
  loop (20) {
    $ix = output.index
    $ad[$ix] = $Hash($K, floor(10 * (3.1 + 17.3 * $ix) + 0.5) / 10)
  }
  $Wd = $width * (1 + $wvar * (2 * $ad[1] - 1))
  $Td = $thick * (1 + $tvar * (2 * $ad[2] - 1))
  $Ld = $length * (1 + $lvar * (2 * $ad[3] - 1))
  $cp = $cup * (0.3 + 0.7 * $ad[7]) * (1 - 2 * clamp(ceil($ad[8] - 0.75), 0, 1))
  $rcap = min(0.3 * $Wd, 0.4 * $Td)
  $ra = min(max($wear * (1 + $wearvar * (2 * $ad[13] - 1)), 0.1 * $wear), $rcap)
  $rb = min(max($wear * (1 + $wearvar * (2 * $ad[14] - 1)), 0.1 * $wear), $rcap)
  $rc = min(0.35 * $wear * (0.6 + 0.8 * $ad[15]), $rcap)
  $rd = min(0.35 * $wear * (0.6 + 0.8 * $ad[16]), $rcap)
  $rm = max($ra, $rb)
  $wa = min($wearvar, 0.8) * (0.3 + 0.7 * $ad[17])
  $wb = min($wearvar, 0.8) * (0.3 + 0.7 * $ad[18])
  $ph = 360 * $ad[19]
  $fr = 0.6 + 1.2 * $ad[20]
  loop (24) {
    $ix = output.index + 20
    $ad[$ix] = $Hash($K, floor(10 * (3.1 + 17.3 * $ix) + 0.5) / 10)
  }
  $dv = clamp($decay * (1 + $state * (2 * $ad[30] - 1)), 0, 1)
  $nck = min(floor($checks * (0.4 + 0.6 * $ad[31]) + 0.5), 3) * clamp(ceil($dv - 0.05), 0, 1)
  $cx1 = 3 + floor(13 * $ad[32])
  $cx2 = 3 + floor(13 * $ad[33])
  $cx3 = 3 + floor(13 * $ad[34])
  $cy1 = 0.05 + 0.3 * $ad[35]
  $cl1 = 0.3 + 0.6 * $ad[36]
  $cy2 = 0.35 + 0.4 * $ad[37]
  $cl2 = 1.0
  $cy3 = 0.0
  $cl3 = 0.15 + 0.4 * $ad[38]
  $sl = clamp(ceil($sliver * $dv - $ad[39]), 0, 1)
  $sly = 0.1 + 0.5 * $ad[40]
  $co = clamp(ceil($corner * $dv - $ad[41]), 0, 1)
  $coe = floor(2 * $ad[42])
  $cos = 2 * floor(2 * $ad[43]) - 1
  $crf = 0.5 + 0.5 * $ad[44]
  $Wd0 = max($Wd, 11.0)
  $Td0 = $Td
  $Wd = $Wd * (1 - $shrink * $dv)
  $Td = $Td * (1 - $thin * $dv)
  $ex0 = (1 - $saw0) * (0.4 * $l0 * $Wd * (1 + $s0 + $v0) + ($h0 + $q0) * $Td + 6.0)
  $ex1 = (1 - $saw1) * (0.4 * $l1 * $Wd * (1 + $s1 + $v1) + ($h1 + $q1) * $Td + 6.0)
  $Ld = $len + $ex0 + $ex1
  if ($dv > 0.001) {
    $NC = 18
    if ($arris > 1.5) {
      add($Kit.DecaySec, w=$Wd, t=$Td, a=max($ra, 0.25), b=max($rb, 0.25), c=$rc, d=$rd, scale=(1.0, $Ld / 100.0, 1.0))
    } else {
      add($Kit.DecaySecG, w=$Wd, t=$Td, a=max($ra, 0.25), b=max($rb, 0.25), c=$rc, d=$rd, scale=(1.0, $Ld / 100.0, 1.0))
    }
    place(by=(0.0, -$ex0, 0.0))
  } else {
    if ($arris > 1.5) {
      add($Kit.AgedSec3, w=$Wd, t=$Td, a=$ra, b=$rb, c=$rc, d=$rd, seg=$seg, scale=(1.0, $Ld / 100.0, 1.0), at=(0.0, -$ex0, 0.0))
    } else {
      add($Kit.AgedSec1, w=$Wd, t=$Td, a=$ra, b=$rb, c=$rc, d=$rd, seg=$seg, scale=(1.0, $Ld / 100.0, 1.0), at=(0.0, -$ex0, 0.0))
    }
  }
  if ($saw0 < 0.5) {
    $Dmg.SnapOff(width=$Wd0, thick=$Td0, deep=$l0, grain=$r0, lean=$q0, layers=2, rings=0, uneven=0.4, rough=1.0, long=$s0, vdep=$v0, horn=$h0, torn=$t0, torntilt=$torntilt, tornrib=$tornrib, tornsep=$tornsep, loss=0.0, chew=0.05, detail=$detail, noise=$n0, origin=(0.0, 0.0, 0.0), rotation=(0.0, 0.0, $a0), uvfit=2, tile=$tile, aspect=$aspect)
  }
  if ($saw1 < 0.5) {
    if ($far > 0.5) {
      $Dmg.SnapOff(width=$Wd0, thick=$Td0, deep=$l1, grain=$r1, lean=$q1, layers=2, rings=0, uneven=0.4, rough=1.0, long=$s1, vdep=$v1, horn=$h1, torn=$t1, torntilt=$torntilt, tornrib=$tornrib, tornsep=$tornsep, loss=0.0, chew=0.05, detail=$detail, noise=$n1, origin=(0.0, $len, 0.0), rotation=(0.0, 0.0, 180.0 + $a1), uvfit=2, tile=$tile, aspect=$aspect)
    } else {
      $Dmg.Snap(width=$Wd0, thick=$Td0, deep=$l1, grain=$r1, lean=$q1, layers=2, rings=0, uneven=0.4, rough=1.0, long=$s1, vdep=$v1, horn=$h1, torn=$t1, torntilt=$torntilt, tornrib=$tornrib, tornsep=$tornsep, loss=0.0, chew=0.05, detail=$detail, noise=$n1, origin=(0.0, $len, 0.0), rotation=(0.0, 0.0, $a1), uvfit=2, tile=$tile, aspect=$aspect)
    }
  }
  keep(largest)
  if ($split > 0.5) {
    $Dmg.Split(width=$Wd0, thick=$Td0, open=0.06, wedge=0.0, length=$len + 2 * $ex0 + 2 * $ex1, close=0.0, detail=1.2 * $detail, noise=$n0 + 5, origin=(($sx - 0.5) * $Wd, $len + $ex1, 0.0))
    keep(largest)
  }
  if ($dv > 0.001) {
    place(by=(0.0, $ex0, 0.0))
    $Kit.Decay(w=$Wd, t=$Td, len=$Ld, a=max($ra, 0.25), b=max($rb, 0.25), dv=$dv, ridge=$ridge, ph=$ph, cd1=clamp(ceil($nck - 0.5), 0, 1) * $checkd * $Td * $dv, cd2=clamp(ceil($nck - 1.5), 0, 1) * $checkd * $Td * $dv, cd3=clamp(ceil($nck - 2.5), 0, 1) * min(1.6 * $checkd, 0.85) * $Td * $dv, cx1=$cx1, cx2=$cx2, cx3=$cx3, cy1=$cy1, cl1=$cl1, cy2=$cy2, cl2=$cl2, cy3=$cy3, cl3=$cl3, crumb=$crumb * $dv, crf=$crf, sl=$sl, sly=$sly, co=$co, coe=$coe, cos=$cos, nc=$NC, softv=$softness)
    if ($groove * $dv > 0.001) {
      $Kit.Grooves(w=$Wd, t=$Td, a=max($ra, 0.25), b=max($rb, 0.25), nc=$NC, dv=$dv, gd=$groove, gs=$gshare, ph=$ph)
    }
    if (($gouge + $lips + $hollow + $edgew) * $dv > 0.001) {
      $Kit.Gouges(w=$Wd, t=$Td, len=$Ld, a=max($ra, 0.25), b=max($rb, 0.25), nc=$NC, dv=$dv, gd=$gouge, lp=$lips, hd=$hollow, ew=$edgew, k=$K + 17)
    }
    place(by=(0.0, -$ex0, 0.0))
  }
  $Kit.Age(w=$Wd, t=$Td, len=$len, cupv=$cp, rm=$rm * (1 - clamp(ceil($dv - 0.001), 0, 1)), wa=$wa, wb=$wb, ph=$ph, fr=$fr, softv=$softness)
  if (max(1 - $saw0 * $saw1, $split) > 0.5) {
    uv(box, facing=(0, 0, 1), up=(0, $Uf, 0), scale=($aspect * $tile, $tile, $tile), offset=($Uo, $Vo)) [!cut]
    if (1 > 0.5) {
      uv(box, facing=(0, 0, 1), up=(0, $Uf, 0), scale=($aspect * $tile, $tile, $tile), offset=($Uo + 0.37, $Vo + 0.61)) [cut]
    }
    material($Face)
    material($Broken) [cut]
  } else {
    uv(box, facing=(0, 0, 1), up=(0, $Uf, 0), scale=($aspect * $tile, $tile, $tile), offset=($Uo, $Vo))
    material($Face)
  }
  # centred on its own origin, then tilted (tl, about its width) or set on its edge (ed, about its length)
  place(by=(0.0, -0.5 * $len, 0.0), rotate=($tl, $ed, 0.0))
}

# ---- the module -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Deck = mesh(size_x=200.0, size_y=200.0, damage=1.0, age=1.0, noise=1, budget=1, softness=0.0, board_w=14.0, board_t=2.6, board_gap=0.3, joists=5, joist_w=3.8, joist_d=18.4, fseed=5, wjit=0.15, gapmin=0.1, gapmax=0.8, egap=0.3, einset=0.05, eivar=0.6, pnone=0.2, ptwo=0.35, bgmin=0.15, bgmax=0.4, bvar=0.015, tvar=0.05, yaw=0.5, lift=0.15, cup=0.3, bow=0.25, crook=0.25, endsq=1.5, wear=0.5, wearvar=0.6, jvw=0.05, jvd=0.03, jsag=0.4, jcrook=0.3, shade=0.15, btwist=0.5, btaper=0.03, bwaney=0.0, bttaper=0.04, bpitch=0.15, broll=0.3, decay=-1.0, dstate=0.35, ridge=0.45, checks=3, checkd=0.45, crumb=4.0, sliver=0.6, corner=0.45, thin=0.15, shrink=0.06, bsag=0.8, plift=0.08, liftc=2.5, missing=1, hole_x=0.5, hole_y=0.5, hole_rx=55.0, hole_ry=35.0, cvar=25.0, svar=0.25, jump=0.1, midbay=0.42, pshort=0.4, gmin=18.0, survive=2, ssag=2.5, plevel=0.6, phang=0.25, pcrack=0.1, hlo=15.0, hhi=45.0, clo=5.0, chi=15.0, slo=60.0, shi=80.0, stub=1, nmin=10.0, nmax=15.0, nlo=35.0, nhi=45.0, rimfrag=1, rimchips=4, long=0.5, deep=0.75, ldeep=1.3, splint=1.0, slant=12.0, grain=0.24, lean=1.6, horn=0.3, rings=0, torn=0.85, torntilt=0.15, tornrib=1, tornsep=0.15, uvbox=1, detail=0.14, hdetail=0.12, jdetail=0.3, tile=100.0, aspect=1.0, jdecay=1.0, jcheck=0.35, jends=0.6, sease=0.05, sthru=1, stones=0, stonesz=7.0, groove=0.0, gshare=0.35, ties=0, tie_w=14.0, gouge=0.0, lips=0.0, hollow=0.0, grit=0, rope=0, edgew=0.0, stonesc=0, ropes=3, tiep=1.0, tieat=3, missp=1.0, tiein=0.0, tiex=0.0) {
