  # round 9 (R3, the lead: "scattered single stones and grit", not tidy piles): `stones` stones about `stonesz` cm, each
  # dropped on its own place over a plank (a share of them in a loose drift toward one side), and `grit` small
  # stones 1-3 cm; every one SETTLED (G31) on the planks, resting on what is under it; round 13: the cluster's stones are
